INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Mandiant: Zero-Day Vulnerability in MOVEit Transfer Exploited for Data Theft; NVD CVE-2023-34362", "source_url": "https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa23-158a; https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/cve-2023-34362", "text": "SRC-001 reports Progress announced the MOVEit Transfer vulnerability on May 31, 2023 and assigned CVE-2023-34362; earliest observed exploitation was May 27, 2023, involving web-shell deployment and data theft. Mandiant says attackers deployed the LEMURLOOT C# web shell, often masquerading as human.aspx, after SQL-injection-directed POST requests to guestaccess.aspx. LEMURLOOT could enumerate files/folders, retrieve configuration and Azure Blob settings, retrieve files, and create/delete a Health Check Service user. Scanning/exploitation often came from 5.252.188.0/22; second-stage systems differed and many hosted RDP with certificates generated May 19-22. Mandiant initially attributed activity to UNC4857, then on June 6 merged UNC4857 into FIN11 based on targeting, infrastructure, certificate, and data-leak-site overlaps. Mandiant reports a June 6 CL0P^_-LEAKS post claiming responsibility and threatening publication unless an extortion fee was paid; a June 5 Bleeping Computer report said a CLOP-affiliated person claimed responsibility. Mandiant says the activity resembled prior FIN11-attributed data-theft extortion involving the CL0P^_-LEAKS site, including Accellion FTA and GoAnywhere MFT exploitation. It had not directly observed extortion emails to confirmed victims and labels delayed ransom-email timing as plausible, not confirmed. SRC-002 describes CVE-2023-34362 as an unauthenticated SQL injection in vulnerable MOVEit Transfer versions, potentially allowing database access and SQL alteration/deletion; exploitation in the wild occurred in May and June 2023 via HTTP/HTTPS. NVD lists CVSS 3.1 9.8 Critical and CISA KEV inclusion with a June 2, 2023 date added and June 23 due date."}
